.TH ZCF 1 "October 2026" "ZCF 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zcf \- Zyntrix Compatibility Fabric universal runtime orchestrator and diagnostics engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zcf
[\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGUMENTS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zcf
is an open-source, distribution-independent application compatibility platform.
It inspects executable binaries (Windows PE, Linux ELF, macOS Mach-O, Android APK),
evaluates hardware and operating system constraints, plans execution through optimal
runtimes (Native, Wine, Proton, QEMU, Box64, Waydroid), applies security sandboxing,
and diagnoses runtime failures with automated remediation recommendations.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B dashboard
Displays the interactive terminal dashboard showing system architecture, detected runtimes, and database status.
.TP
.B console \fR[\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR] [\fB\-\-host\fR \fIHOST\fR]
Launches the secure loopback browser-based Web Console and REST API. (Alias: \fBweb\fR).
.TP
.B gui
Launches the standalone graphical Control Center for desktop application and prefix management.
.TP
.B run \fIPATH\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
Executes an application through its optimal planned runtime, ensuring prefix isolation, sandboxing, and automated crash diagnostics.
.TP
.B integrate \fIPATH\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\fR]
Manages Freedesktop application menu launchers with proper Exec escaping and reversible unintegration.
.TP
.B service \fIaction\fR
Manages system integration and background maintenance (\fBregister\-binfmt\fR, \fBunregister\-binfmt\fR, \fBcleanup\-prefixes\fR, \fBlist\-prefixes\fR).
.TP
.B inspect \fIPATH\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Performs non-executing static analysis of a binary or script, extracting architecture, subsystem, imports, and Authenticode signatures.
.TP
.B env [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Audits the host environment and detects installed compatibility runtimes.
.TP
.B plan \fIPATH\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Generates a deterministic compatibility plan with explainable confidence scoring.
.TP
.B test \fIPATH\fR [\fB\-\-dry-run\fR] [\fB\-\-execute\fR] [\fB\-\-record\fR]
Validates execution capability in an isolated test harness and optionally records evidence to the database.
.TP
.B diag \fILOG_PATH\fR [\fB\-\-target\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Analyzes execution failure logs against known failure signatures and synthesizes distribution-tailored fix commands.
.TP
.B research \fIBINARY_PATH\fR \fILOG_PATH\fR
Executes the 11-step empirical reverse-engineering and hypothesis verification workflow.
.TP
.B db \fIaction\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Manages the compatibility knowledge base. Actions include \fBlist\fR, \fBshow\fR, \fBquery\fR, \fBsubmit\fR, \fBverify\fR, \fBdelete\fR, \fBexport\fR, and \fBimport\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B ZCF_PREFIX_DIR
Overrides the root directory for managed runtime prefixes (default: \fI~/.local/share/zcf/prefixes\fR).
.TP
.B ZCF_SANDBOX
Controls Bubblewrap sandboxing. Set to \fB0\fR or \fBoff\fR to disable sandboxing.
.TP
.B ZCF_HEADLESS
Forces execution inside an automated virtual framebuffer (\fBxvfb\fR) even if a physical display is available.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/binfmt.d/zcf.conf
Systemd binfmt_misc kernel registration for transparent binary execution.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/org.zyntrix.zcf.desktop
Freedesktop XDG application launcher.
